# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# ── Your data never goes to GitHub ──────────────────────────────────────────
# RoomKit is a private inventory of your own room. The code is safe to publish;
# what the app stores about you is not. These are the only paths that ever hold
# personal content, and they stay on the machine that created them.
#
# Photos you took of your own belongings.
/public/uploads/

# Orphaned state from the old auto-sync backend, kept locally until you delete
# it. It is a complete dump of your inventory.
#
# The leading slash matters: a bare `data/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, which silently swallows src/data/ and src/features/data/ -- real
# source code that must be in the repo.
/data/

# Dated snapshots written by desktop archiving. A complete dump of the
# inventory, so it stays on the machine that made it.
/backups/

# Exports from the "Export Database Backup" button, wherever they land.
my-room-backup*.json
*.backup.json
roomkit-backup*.json

# ── Editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .vscode is deliberately NOT ignored: launch.json and tasks.json are what make
# F5 start the whole app, so they belong in the repo. Only per-user editor
# state is excluded.
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/*.log
.history

.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Secrets, if you ever add any (ngrok tokens, API keys)
.env
.env.*

# Deploy tooling scratch (created by `vercel` and `wrangler`)
.vercel
.wrangler

# Keep the template that documents which vars are needed. This must stay
# last: a later `.env*` rule would otherwise swallow it again.
!.env.example
